# The image is the service, not the repo checkout. `COPY *.py .` in the Dockerfile picks up every
# module by glob so a new source file can never be forgotten — this file is what keeps that glob
# from also shipping the unit tests and local build residue (RELEASE-DECISIONS N12: "test modules
# leave the image").
test_*.py
conftest.py
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
*.md
.dockerignore
